ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068813 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050699 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068814 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050699 #edb/ref 1031 "Combining Graph Transformations of Reciprocal Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050699 #edb/ref 1033 455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050699 #edb/ref 1034 1.2244606727212959 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050699 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5fe705bb-18d4-531c-8614-9f3d188aa2c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068619 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5924" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068619 #edb/ref 1071 "Graph the function $y = -\\dfrac{2}{x-1}-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068619 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d86c6bd2-e528-55ed-bbfc-9f5ecbec024e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068619 #edb/ref 1074 "To plot $y = -\\dfrac{2}{x-1}-1,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/9d/9da0db2e6c97e507e82b7ca801e46802fabf91ad31ff53ad3cc9ae580151370a.png)\n\n- Translate it by one unit to the right to get the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x-1}.$ \n\n![](images/8c/8ce8c53f202f04b3b34a247b797f65f7616e8772afa1751de126ddd401417bd7.png)\n\nNotice that the vertical asymptote is now $x=1.$\n\n- Then, stretch the result by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{2}{x-1}.$\n\n![](images/c9/c9b708a20d9c6c12f0016279e8d7a3ea55597e7645f0a9518f1c32e8a8406e47.png)\n\n- Finally, translate it by $1$ unit down to get the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{2}{x-1}-1.$ \n\n![](images/e1/e100b552adb71cae1295492a58b0e60525813adb87d9815ba64a151a856f0c46.png)\n\nNotice that the horizontal asymptote is now $y=-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068620 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5926" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068620 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/fb/fb46d056a8d8010eca509543c231c875f4980a21f1af17505fa98c8c64106207.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the graph of $y = \\dfrac{a}{x-b}+k.$ What is the value of $a+b+k?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068620 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ac8b39e3-a9d0-56fd-8c0b-4d748bedf7d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068620 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=-1,$ while the vertical asymptote is $x=2.$ This means that $k=-1$ and $b=2,$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{a}{x-2}+(-1) = \\dfrac{a}{x-2}-1.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(3,2)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x-2}-1 \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{a}{3-2}-1 \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{a}{1} \\\\ a & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b+k = 3+2+(-1) = 4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068655 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8658" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068655 #edb/ref 1071 "Sketch the graph of $y = \\dfrac{7}{2x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068655 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a76e0252-0574-520e-bb5f-43c8faf6a564" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068655 #edb/ref 1074 "To plot $y = \\dfrac{7}{2x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\dfrac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/e8/e80865b0f32a5473da27b39537034bcdabee0a6c24032f41413e20518642d3f4.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\dfrac{7}{2}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\dfrac{7}{2x}.$\n\n![](images/b7/b7b1fe93de798c0aa91f60f66a2507869dbe837b843b7233972e1a78ee22576a.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068656 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8761" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068656 #edb/ref 1071 "Sketch the graph of $y = -\\dfrac{1}{5x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068656 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a18ff1e7-7f87-5cdd-9a25-91a2e9c1dd5b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068656 #edb/ref 1074 "To plot $y = -\\dfrac{1}{5x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/d5/d5d93e12275c683e0a56f0ec9a0c99540a7774879cd0f8fa69151ddba68a44fa.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\dfrac 1 5$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{5x}.$\n\n![](images/30/30ace3126ec127b9949ebf599d615020b9770458825d22460e9e7e0b3d5efec3.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068779 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068779 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068779 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068779 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068779 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068779 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068779 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068779 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068779 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068779 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068779 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186395370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068779 #edb/ref 1039 "Graphing a Transformed Reciprocal Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068779 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068779 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "4640f978-9caa-5960-bec4-f153a1b4cc5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068780 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068780 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069318 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068780 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068780 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068780 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068780 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068780 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068780 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068780 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186562395 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068780 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186562424 #edb