fe5c1fe17b9fa8b62fe9f33e052eb295161ce7a368047111.svg) we start with the graph of ![](images/f3/f39b65736426b97929738170b1a75a6aac5ba9cfbad1b444a65098297b7b1d63.svg) and stretch it by a scale factor of ![](images/6c/6cb44f25e489afb06ec62d2e95c4d235ece77eb36e2327b856264d2fb8b22c21.svg) parallel to the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/d0/d01107a224cc4a12f05263a7f159c8ad25a04ff061e1eda3045113e6671f0113.png)\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The point ![](images/0c/0c733476e5ce2ef628b2dd5447582a6e69de8d045147925a803dcfb6e9834a0c.svg) on ![](images/f3/f39b65736426b97929738170b1a75a6aac5ba9cfbad1b444a65098297b7b1d63.svg) is mapped to the point ![](images/c8/c8d810917eef2cc68b3c133405d6aa3fe648c64b6f8e50cc1a0bcc4eb84ba536.svg) on ![](images/62/62dc824c36f1634a45236f35fa955f7b7863996ea26708e7e4295d0a73e258be.svg)\n\n- The point ![](images/c1/c18723d4a2788ff033587f5be97e6a0b50d886a8f74a130c92eb348d2a6498b9.svg) on ![](images/f3/f39b65736426b97929738170b1a75a6aac5ba9cfbad1b444a65098297b7b1d63.svg) is mapped to the point ![](images/c9/c9629cfe801a15e75ff1548b053d4507fc7bff739ce77315e64cf5bb7fd6bd21.svg) on ![](images/62/62dc824c36f1634a45236f35fa955f7b7863996ea26708e7e4295d0a73e258be.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069978 #edb/ref 1065 3766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069978 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f6acc898-4f1c-5323-89f4-13283701fda1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069978 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069986 #edb/ref 1064 "Similarly, to sketch the graph of $y=\\dfrac{1}{2x},$ we take the graph of $y=\\dfrac1x$ and stretch it by a scale factor of $\\dfrac12$ parallel to the $y$-axis.\n\n![](images/08/08c02826d4c2dff684e00c01e9229e5ef7767f4122d99fcfa8e5d63c254cbd94.png)\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The point $(1,1)$ on $y=\\dfrac1x$ is mapped to the point $\\left(1,\\dfrac12\\right)$ on $y=\\dfrac{1}{2x}.$\n\n- The point $(-1,-1)$ on $y=\\dfrac1x$ is map