ion" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562263 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186561787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562263 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3cf5df72-e286-51fa-b6b6-9ce9d54e2f6e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562266 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562266 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562266 #edb/ref 1077 "field-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562266 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186561916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562266 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "40d7c4e5-3f33-5e32-a43f-784a1408b1a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562273 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562273 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562273 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562273 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186561751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562273 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4f66befd-be45-5c10-a46a-921be5c7d226" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562310 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562310 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562310 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562310 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186561643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562310 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "887368ab-3a85-523d-a904-ef84af68ef2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562366 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562366 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562366 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562366 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562197 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562366 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562366 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562366 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562366 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186562206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562366 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e202ebbd-74b7-50fc-8387-e3cfbc2ec9ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562395 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562395 #edb/ref 1069 "q-113475" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562395 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562395 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/fc/fc0ad365fca91e61da2e7f09197299ea6130018d7490873d3568231be360b481.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the graph of $y=\\frac{a}{x}.$ What is the value of $a?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562395 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0afab3eb-630e-58a0-8be5-5f624db42ba7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562395 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that the point $(3,-1)$ lies on the graph.\n\nSubstituting its coordinates into the equation $y=\\frac{a}{x},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1=\\frac{a}{3}\\,⟹\\,a=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562424 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562424 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562424 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562424 #edb/ref 1069 "q-270753" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562424 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562424 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/84/84c4df89c98cd103049ac6161c5d3e4eec258d3ecb3c1af94bf7d300f9342d22.png)\n\nThe graph represents the function $y=\\frac{a}{x-b}+k.$ What are the values of $a,$ $b,$ and $k?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}},$\\,b=$\n{{field-2}},$\\,k=$\n{{field-3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562424 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3ce08e84-b291-5c5a-ac58-9e142f6fb8a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562424 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=1.5,$ while the vertical asymptote is $x=-1.$ This means that $k=1.5$ and $b=-1,$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{a}{x-(-1)}+1.5=\\frac{a}{x+1}+1.5.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(1,3.5)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x+1}+1.5 \\\\ 3.5 & =\\frac{a}{1+1}+1.5 \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{a}{2} \\\\ a & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562443 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562366 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562443 #edb/ref 1069 "q-99063" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562443 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562443 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\frac{4}{x}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562443 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "71350d61-9672-52ac-9492-4bd38fc59f6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562443 #edb/ref 1074 "To plot $y=\\frac{4}{x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/b3/b3a79a8dbe82342c0ab1e16371f8c1d82833f4ebc3bad659f1a619ab1e92733e.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $4$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{4}{x}.$\n\n![](images/e1/e10be40920aebaaf2f5984e25cff2143ee145851d5feaef48df883cf3556cacc.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562452 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562452 #edb/ref 1069 "q-113320" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562452 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562452 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{5x}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562452 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "821ebc7d-79c0-5cb4-8fa5-4c72551d87fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562452 #edb/ref 1074 "To plot $y=\\frac{1}{5x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/0f/0fe642f3c7873344885b0e030fb449a8bf882120e675f18d72668ccae3ef4b40.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{5}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{5x}.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c7b719326bfa1a4b53fdf2bce3f6e7f1dafe5de2c994ffb4951a6d79af78707.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562477 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562477 #edb/ref 1069 "q-97964" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562477 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562477 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\frac{2}{5x}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562477 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b235c15c-2f59-5a6f-acea-69e0a744bdcd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562477 #edb/ref 1074 "To plot $y=-\\frac{2}{5x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/d5/d5d93e12275c683e0a56f0ec9a0c99540a7774879cd0f8fa69151ddba68a44fa.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{2}{5}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{2}{5x}.$\n\n![](images/22/22a5600f9104cbb34a4274f09af767862e7b7bc21dc2edbca2a55e5207947142.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562480 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562480 #edb/ref 1069 "q-113334" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562480 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562480 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\frac{5}{x}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562480 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b38c16c9-634c-5bda-ac99-e07bc23505a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562480 #edb/ref 1074 "To plot $y=-\\frac{5}{x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/d5/d5d93e12275c683e0a56f0ec9a0c99540a7774879cd0f8fa69151ddba68a44fa.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $5$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{5}{x}.$\n\n![](images/7c/7ce9a42f05beeebb422c49e34670513a65a7183a51bd49fb2354e72f0942513e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
